design:
SLICE 4 ENGINE AND CHECKS (core + runner): THE TRANSFORM

0. PRINCIPLES
- One draft, one analysis, one planner. A transform is data (TransformDraft). analyseTransform (pure) answers TR-11/G6, TR-12 (a), TR-13, TR-15 and RV-5 b3. planTypedWrite (pure) turns the draft into file changes plus the list of units it wrote. Outside a session the plan is a board action (one Undo step). Inside a session it is the first commit of a queue step of kind 'transform'.
- Reuse, never parallel:
  - from slice 2: the queue (D2-63), StepScope and the step limits (existing-changed against S0), judgeState, computeItems, reconcile, reduceReview with the session stack, the write queue, planSubmit with D2-57's take-out, the base mask, the backstop and the end confirmation;
  - from slice 3: effectiveFreezes, frozenFindings with its two-value rule, frozenChangesOf (D3-48), the whole-model tools and G5 allowances, and the hooks of §3.12.
- Prefer refusing: stale drafts, typed states that do not build, frozen dependents, and transforms touching a session target's proof are refused with a sentence.
- Yours is unforgeable: telelean records every unit it wrote for you in a ledger entry outside ws/, and a unit counts as yours only while the judged state holds exactly that value.

1. DATA MODEL (core src/transform/types.ts, 4a1)
type FieldState = 'frozen' | 'open' | 'fuzzy' | 'keep-empty';   // TR-4; keep-empty = frozen empty (FZ-2)
type DraftKey = string;   // existing card id | fully qualified vocab name | 'new:<n>' (a card made in the window)
interface DraftValue<V> {
  value: V | null; from: V | null; state: FieldState;
  /** TR-15/DO-2: the copied value is Claude's proposal (an item's content); starts open (D4-7). */
  claude?: { item: string; rev: number };
  /** Frozen by a reason outside the window (standing, session-start, accepted, yours): the window cannot open it; Unfreeze first (FZ-6). */
  heldBy?: FreezeReasonView[];
}
interface DraftCard {
  key: DraftKey; origin: 'copy' | 'new' | 'premise';
  premise?: { item: string; rev: number; target: string };          // D4-11
  kind: DraftValue<NodeType>;                                         // never fuzzy (TR-2 b); a change is TR-11
  sentence: DraftValue<string>; why: DraftValue<string>; stance: DraftValue<Stance>; source: DraftValue<Evidential>;
  statement: DraftValue<string>;                                       // the abbrev's proposition text
  dependencies?: DraftValue<{ sources: DraftKey[]; fromNothing: boolean }>;   // PROPOSITION only; edited as per-arrow diffs
  proof?: { state: 'empty' | 'pending' | 'proved'; clear: boolean; locked?: string };   // TR-4: keep or clear; locked = D4-16
  trashed: boolean;                                                    // TR-3
}
interface DraftVocab { key: DraftKey; origin: 'copy' | 'new'; declaration: DraftValue<string>; gloss: DraftValue<string>; trashed: boolean }
type TransformFrom = { kind: 'cards' } | { kind: 'decline'; items: Array<{ item: string; rev: number }> }
  | { kind: 'ask-me'; items: Array<{ item: string; rev: number }>; choice: string };   // D2-13
interface TransformDraft {
  id: string; subject: string; from: TransformFrom;
  /** Outside a session: B's file hashes. In a session: the stage judgement's commit and viewVersion. */
  basis: { files?: Record<string, string>; commit?: string; viewVersion?: number };
  cards: DraftCard[]; vocab: DraftVocab[];
  mayAddCards: boolean;            // TR-7 (a), default false
  instructions: string;            // TR-8 (# references: slice 5)
  dependents: Record<string, DependentChoice>;    // TR-13 choices by card id or Lean name
  revision: number;
}
type DependentChoice = 'claude' | 'delete' | 'rewrite' | 'broken';   // rewrite and broken: outside a session only (D4-19)
interface TransformAnalysis {
  draft: { id: string; revision: number };
  changed: boolean;                         // TR-1 (b)
  needsClaude: NeedsClaudeReason[];         // TR-15; empty = needs no Claude
  problems: TransformProblem[];             // block Submit transform
  warnings: TransformProblem[];             // TR-13 b2 etc.
  dependents: TransformDependent[];         // TR-13 b1
  kinds: Array<{ card: DraftKey; from: NodeType; to: NodeType; impact: KindChangeImpact;
    removedArrows: Array<ArrowEnds & { frozen: FreezeReasonView[] }>; removedMark?: { frozen: FreezeReasonView[] } }>;   // TR-11 + G6
  verbatim: Array<{ card: DraftKey; names: string[]; proposedInSession: string[] }>;   // TR-12 (c), D4-5
  freezes: { transform: FreezeTarget[]; revalue: FreezeKey[] };                         // FZ-7 r4, FZ-3 2e
  session?: { touched: string[]; acceptedCascade: CascadeEntry[]; reworkResults: string[] };   // RV-5 b3; never a hidden item
  leanChecked?: string;                     // hash of the typed Lean texts TR-12 (b) checked
}
type NeedsClaudeReason = { why: 'fuzzy'; card: DraftKey; field: string } | { why: 'instructions' } | { why: 'add-cards' }
  | { why: 'sentence-open-lean'; card: DraftKey } | { why: 'verbatim'; card: DraftKey; names: string[] }
  | { why: 'dependents'; cards: string[] } | { why: 'slot'; card: DraftKey };
interface TransformDependent { of: DraftKey; dependent: string; via: 'arrow' | 'proof' | 'statement' | 'definition' | 'reference';
  frozen: FreezeReasonView[]; choices: DependentChoice[] }

Additions to the review model (core review/types.ts, 4a1, additive):
- ItemKind: + 'typed'. Key `typed:<card id | Lean name>` (keys.ts typedKey; parseItemKey). There is one per card, holding every live typed unit on that card (D4-1).
- LedgerEntry: + `{ kind: 'typed'; transform: string; step: string; units: TypedUnit[]; commit?: string }`.
- TypedUnit, each with the value telelean wrote:
  - `{ kind: 'field'; card; field: 'sentence'|'why'|'stance'|'source'|'kind'|'mark'; value: string|null }`;
  - `{ kind: 'statement'; card; name; text: string|null }`, which includes the docstring mirror, the pin and an AXIOM's .holds;
  - `{ kind: 'holds'; card; text: string|null }`, for P→A's axiom and a cleared proof;
  - `{ kind: 'arrow'; source; target; present: boolean }`;
  - `{ kind: 'card'; card; present: boolean }`, for a new block or a trashed card with its follow-on arrow removals;
  - `{ kind: 'decl'; name; text: string|null }`, for vocabulary, the gloss included;
  - `{ kind: 'premise-edit'; item; sentence?; statement?; why? }`, which changes records only (D4-11).
- ItemRecord.accepted.how: + 'yours'. ItemMarker: + 'typed-by-you' | 'replaced-by-transform'.
- StepScope: + `transform?: TransformScope`. For a transform step, `target` holds `transform:<id>` and is never a card id. `openProof` and `openArrows` are false.
interface TransformScope {
  id: string; claude: boolean; rework?: true;
  fields: Array<{ card: string; field: 'sentence'|'why'|'stance'|'source'|'statement'; mode: 'fuzzy'|'open' }>;
  vocab: Array<{ name: string; field: 'declaration'|'gloss'; mode: 'fuzzy'|'open' }>;
  arrowsInto: Array<{ card: string; mode: 'fuzzy'|'open' }>;      // B.3 transform
  verbatim: Array<{ card: string; text: string }>;                // TR-12 (c)
  slots: Array<{ slot: string; kind: NodeType; id: string }>;     // D4-12
  mayAddCards: boolean;                                            // TR-7 (a), at most 10 add_card calls per step
  dependents: { statements: string[]; proofs: string[] };          // TR-13 left to Claude
  instructions: string;
}
- PersistedStep (runner): kind + 'transform'. It also gains `typedCommit?` (S0 for the limits), keeps `startCommit` (the rollback target) and adds `transform: string`. StepView.kind + 'transform'. SessionPhase is unchanged: no 'drafting' phase (D4-2).
- SessionAction: + `{ id; kind: 'transform'; op: 'queue'|'drop'|'replace'; label; transform; before: QueuedTransform|null; after: QueuedTransform|null; changes: Array<{ item; rev; before: ItemState; after: ItemState }>; at }`.
- ReviewAction: + `{ kind: 'queue-transform'; transform: QueuedTransformInput; replaces?: string; confirmed: boolean }` and `{ kind: 'drop-transform'; transform: string; confirmed: boolean }`. The reducer accepts DeclineOption 'transform' only inside queue-transform.
- PersistedSession (run.json v2, additive):
  - `startedBy?: 'formalize'|'transform'`;
  - `openDraft?: { draft: TransformDraft; analysis?: TransformAnalysis }` (ES-6; one window at a time);
  - `transforms: QueuedTransform[]`, where `QueuedTransform = { draft; analysis; queuedBy: number; state: 'queued'|'running'|'done'; lastFailure?: string; steps: string[] }`.
- Slice 3's freeze types (4a1, additive):
  - FreezeReason 'transform' gains `transform: string`.
  - `SessionFreezes.start` gains `transform?: { selected: { cards: string[]; vocab: string[] } }`.
  - `startCleared?: FreezeKey[]` (an Unfreeze of a session-start reason, per key).
  - `transform?: TransformFreeze[]`, with `TransformFreeze = { target: FreezeTarget; transform: string; at: string; value: OwnValue | { pending: true } }`.
  - `revalued?: { keys: Record<FreezeKey, OwnValue>; held: Record<string, HeldValue> }`.
  - FreezeDelta per key gains `startCleared?` and `transform?`, so Undo of an Unfreeze restores them.
- Views (core review/view.ts):
  - `SessionView.transforms: TransformView[]`, each with label, cards, needsClaude, sources, state and lastFailure;
  - `SessionView.openDraft`;
  - `SessionFreezesView.start.transform`, for FZ-11's banner "Everything except the selected cards is frozen";
  - `EndConfirmationView.typed: Array<{ card; label; units: Array<{ field; before; after }> }>` (EN-2 Apply b2);
  - ItemView for 'typed' items.
- core actions.ts:
  - BoardAction + `{ kind: 'apply-transform'; subject: string; draft: TransformDraft; confirmed?: { dependents?: true; glow?: true; kinds?: Record<string, DependentsChoice> } }`;
  - HistoryActionKind + 'apply-transform', with labels in runner workspace/history.ts and webview labels.ts.
- LIMITS: transformCards 50, transformVocab 50, draftBytes 256000, transformsQueued 50; instructions use textLength.

2. CORE FUNCTIONS (signatures)
- makeTransformDraft(i: { model: ProjectModel; graph: TlGraph; subject; cards: string[]; vocab: string[]; from: TransformFrom; freezes: Record<FreezeKey, FreezeReasonView[]>; session?: { targets: string[]; resultsShown: boolean; items: ItemView[] } }): TransformDraft. It copies field values and states: texts from the model's files, derived states from the (masked) graph. It applies TR-4 starting states:
  - your copied Sentence, Why, Stance and Source are open;
  - Lean statement, Dependencies and Proof are frozen (S11);
  - empty fields are keep-empty;
  - Claude's proposed values are open and marked (D4-7);
  - fields frozen by another reason carry heldBy;
  - a session target's proof is locked (D4-16).
  It refuses another subject's vocabulary (TR-10 c), a Result, an arrow item and a Proof broken item (D4-21).
- typedLeanProblems(draft, model): TransformProblem[] (TR-12 a, pure):
  - A statement must pass G0's termProblems: single term, no command words, no comment delimiters, no #commands, no forbidden tokens, balanced brackets, no top-level := or |.
  - A vocabulary declaration must be exactly one declaration (markup/decls.ts) named as the card. Its keyword is in {axiom, def, abbrev, structure, inductive, class, instance, opaque}. No other command. scanForbiddenText finds nothing in it, including init and hygienic names (AP30-1).
  - An axiom must pass the shape rule (shapeOf). A Prop axiom bound to no card is refused (D2-40): "add an axiom card instead". A theorem is refused (TR-14).
- analyseTransform(i: { draft; model: ProjectModel; graph: TlGraph; scratch?: TypedScratchResult; session?: TransformSessionContext }): TransformAnalysis. It is pure; §3.2–3.4 give its rules.
- planTypedWrite(model, draft, ctx: { today; now; reserved: Set<string>; mode: 'direct'|'session'; session?: { targets: string[] } }): { changes: FileChange[]; units: TypedUnit[]; archive: ArchiveEntry[]; ids: Record<DraftKey, string> }. §3.6.
- planTransformDirect(model, action, ctx: PlanContext): EditPlan. This is the apply-transform case of planAction: planTypedWrite in 'direct' mode plus D3-44 freeze deltas, A6 drops and D-11 confirmations.
- transformScopeOf(draft, analysis, model): TransformScope.
- Extended, not new:
  - computeItems, planItemRevert, reconcile, classify, itemDeps, isMeaningItem;
  - judgeState (transform scope), applyBackstop;
  - effectiveFreezes, frozenFindings, frozenChangesOf, buildFreezesView;
  - reduceReview, planGroupDecline ('transform'), planSubmit, formalizeStartProblems, buildSessionView;
  - the slice-3 tool validators (removeArrowProblems, proofBrokenProblems, addCardProblems, propose_arrow's) with a transform-scope branch.

3. ALGORITHMS
3.1 Opening and drafts (ES-6, RV-6, D4-2, D4-15)
- Outside a session, openTransform is handled by the host alone. It calls makeTransformDraft on the board's model (B) and stores the draft in the host's per-folder storage (workspaceState key `telelean.transformDraft.<subject>`). No run is created and nothing is frozen yet. The draft is saved, debounced, on every change.
- In a session, the runner's transformOpen builds the draft from the stage judgement's model and the view's graph. The graph is masked while the results are hidden, so proof states are as in B and Results' arrows are absent. The draft is stored as `openDraft`: a records-only run.json write, not on the stack, allowed in every phase but confirming (there: "Back to review first").
- Transform cards… on the Current view during a session is disabled: "Transform from the Proposed view".
- Freeze actions inside the window: toggling a draft field's state belongs to the draft. The Context Menu's Freeze actions on cards outside the window are real freeze actions: standing outside a session, session-stack steps inside one (FZ-9).

3.2 Field states and TR-15
- **A field is changed** when its value differs from `from`; for Dependencies, compare arrow by arrow. The transform is changed when a field changed, or a card is new or trashed, or a kind or proof-clear or Dependencies change exists.
- **Typing** freezes the field (TR-5). Clearing makes it fuzzy.
- **needsClaude** (TR-15) when the transform has any of:
  - a fuzzy field;
  - instructions that are not blank;
  - mayAddCards;
  - a changed sentence whose Lean statement is open;
  - a verbatim statement (§3.3);
  - a dependent with choice 'claude';
  - a new card whose sentence is fuzzy (a slot, D4-12).
- A typed arrow may not involve a slot.

3.3 TR-12 (D4-5)
- **(a)** typedLeanProblems runs in the window, at Submit transform, and again in every planner (fail closed).
- **(b) The scratch.** runner semantic/typedScratch.ts generates the source and reads the messages. ModelWorkspace.checkTypedLean runs `lake env lean --stdin --json` at the model root, under the refresh's sandbox, runExclusive and the memory guard. The root holds your files. The board is locked during a session, so this is B. The scratch source is:
  - `import <library>`;
  - `set_option autoImplicit false`, `set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false`;
  - `namespace <S>.telelean_typed`;
  - every typed vocabulary declaration, in draft order, under its short name;
  - every typed statement as `abbrev <its card's statement short name> : Prop := <text>`, ordered by mentions (a cycle is a problem);
  - `end`.
  Inside that namespace, names the transform changes resolve to the typed versions, and every other name to your files.
- **Reading the scratch messages:**
  - messages are attributed by line;
  - "unknown identifier/constant" in a statement means the name is not in your files. If the name is visible session content (Claude's vocabulary in review or accepted), it is listed under proposedInSession;
  - any other error is a problem on that field;
  - a vocabulary declaration with any error is a problem: typed vocabulary must elaborate now.
- **Freshness.** The check is refused when the board's facts are not fresh ("wait for the Lean check of your files") or the files drifted (ES-7).
- **Cost.** One Lean job per Submit transform; never while typing.
- **(c) Verbatim.** A statement with only unknown-name errors is listed in `verbatim`: "Claude must define: …". It is not part of the typed write. The transform step's scope.verbatim carries it. The gate's new rule `typed-text` requires that card's statement text to equal it (whitespace collapsed): "The person typed “‹card›”'s Lean statement as `‹text›`: write exactly that (define what it needs first)." Its transform reason gets its value at the queue end (D4-20).

3.4 TR-13, TR-11, RV-5 b3 (D4-19, D4-10, D4-16)
- **Dependents of each changed or trashed card or declaration.** All are computed from facts:
  - **arrows:** arrows out of a trashed card. They are removed as follow-on edits, listed, and need no choice unless a proof uses them;
  - **proofs:** cards whose direct(v), footprint or proof uses (usersOf, axiomListUsers) reach the changed or trashed .holds or a changed declaration;
  - **statements:** the meaning closure (review/closure.ts reach) of card statements;
  - **definitions:** vocabulary that mentions it;
  - **references:** heldFields() returns [] until slice 5 (RF-5 b).
- **Choices.**
  - In a session: 'claude' (unfrozen only) or 'delete' (trash it too). A frozen dependent is a problem: "‹card› relies on ‹x› and is frozen (‹reasons›): unfreeze it to leave it to Claude, or trash it too."
  - Outside a session: 'delete', 'broken' (today's Delete anyway, which marks dependents broken; TR-13), or 'rewrite' (D-11, only for kind-change dependents of a conditional proof).
- **Session targets** (cards with a Result in the session, D4-16):
  - their proof is locked;
  - trashing one is refused;
  - changing a target's statement is allowed only when B has no proof of it. Its Result is then added to `session.reworkResults`, taken out before the queue (D2-57) and reworked in the same queue.
  - Otherwise the change is refused: "“‹T›” has a proof in your files that this statement change would break: change it after the session."
  - A Result whose proof depends on a changed card is a proof dependent. For a session target, 'claude' means its Result is reworked in this queue.
- **TR-13 b2.** A changed sentence whose Lean statement stays frozen is a warning ("the two may then disagree"). The item is marked c3.
- **TR-11 (with G6).** Each Kind change is analysed:
  - kindChangeImpact runs on the (masked) graph;
  - removedArrows and removedMark name each frozen one with its reasons (standing, session-start, accepted, yours, transform);
  - A→P keeps the axiom as pending (D-11's A→D row, planArrows' helper), with AR-6's glow-loss confirmation;
  - P→A removes incoming arrows and the mark and replaces the proof with `axiom n.holds` (AR-7);
  - in a session, a P→A whose conditional proof has dependents needing D-11's rewrite is refused: "move it to axioms after the session".
- **RV-5 b3 / RV-6 b4.** `session.touched` lists the items owning a unit the plan overwrites or removes. `acceptedCascade` lists the accepted ones plus their accepted RV-5 dependents, from the stage judgement's deps, transitively. While the results are hidden both are computed on the masked state, so they never name a hidden item. At Submit they are recomputed on the real state.

3.5 Submit transform outside a session (ES-3; D4-2)
1. The host refuses a stale draft: basis.files differ from the current files ("Your files changed since you opened the window: Cancel and open it again").
2. It runs analyseTransform with the scratch. Any problem goes back to the window.
3. Unchanged and needs no Claude: start a session (runner transformStart mode 'unchanged'). This makes the base commit and the session-start freezes. Stage 1 is empty with no Claude step, and Formalize can run from it. No consent is needed until the first Claude step (§3.9).
4. Needs Claude: egress consent, then transformStart mode 'claude':
   - preflight, shadow, base commit;
   - session-start freezes;
   - checkBase (B must build, else "fix your files first"; the draft is kept);
   - conversation; context bundle with first line `Run: "Transform cards" for the subject <S> (…)`;
   - a queue-start with one transform step.
   Stage 1 opens when the queue ends.
5. Changed and needs no Claude: the direct path. The host first dry-runs planAction(apply-transform) on the current model, which is pure. It then performs the action through its board queue. One history entry, one Undo step. No run ever existed.
6. Cancel deletes the stored draft. The webview asks first when the draft has any change; no session freezes exist to undo.

3.6 planTypedWrite (shared by both paths)
Composition, on EditSession, in this order:
1. New cards, from the window:
   - a block in the Inbox, with an explicit id from deriveId(typed sentence, reserved = ids of B, W, the ledger, the freeze records (D3-54) and the draft), asserted, session, worded_by user;
   - its typed statement as an abbrev inserted after the block, with a lean: pin, plus `axiom n.holds : n` for an AXIOM (add-holds-axiom);
   - slots (fuzzy sentence) are not written; add_card fills them.
2. New vocabulary: inserted at the end of the subject's Vocabulary.lean namespace, in draft order. Changed vocabulary: replace-decl. Gloss: set-docstring.
3. Field edits (setField). A typed sentence on a worded_by: agent block drops that line (CF-6, G5) and updates the statement's D-9 docstring mirror (D4-21's residual).
4. Typed statements of existing cards: replace-decl of the abbrev, or insert with pin for a card without one.
5. Kind changes, via planKind (P→A) or the A→D helper.
6. Arrows: per-arrow premises entries, with the cycle check (AR-3, AP-13). A mark set or removed (a mark together with arrows is a problem).
7. Cleared proofs: remove-holds with archive (TR-4: unproved, never pending).
8. Trash: delete-node's pieces (block, statement, .holds archived, premise removals elsewhere), or remove-decl for a vocabulary card.
Each written thing becomes a TypedUnit with its exact value.
- **The no-Claude-content rule (TR-15, D4-1).** A unit is recorded only if, after the write, it holds no Claude content: its other parts are B's or earlier typed units'. A change landing in a block line or declaration that holds Claude content is written but not recorded. It stays in Claude's item, which returns to review marked "updated".
- **Direct-mode extras (TR-15 outside a session):**
  - D3-44 deltas freeze each typed field of an existing card as a standing freeze: sentence, why, stance, source, statement, vocab declaration, gloss (D4-13);
  - A6 drops the records of trashed cards and removed arrows and marks;
  - 'broken' and 'rewrite' come from `confirmed`;
  - the layout drops trashed cards' positions;
  - label "Transform: ‹first card› (+N)".

3.7 Transform-started sessions (D3-1 made real, D4-14)
- At transformStart, SessionFreezes.start.transform.selected holds the window's cards and vocab.
- effectiveFreezes derives a 'session-start' entry, expected at B (`{ from: 'base' }`, or revalued), for every card and vocabulary card of the subject not selected. Each is a whole card: all 8 fields and its Dependencies, so arrows into non-selected cards too. Keys in `startCleared` are excluded.
- Unfreeze of such a key adds it to startCleared (one session step). Undo restores it.
- FZ-8: session-start reasons end with the session. EN-2's summary line counts them.
- frozenNeeds (slice 3 §3.11) warns when a later mid-stage Formalize targets a session-start-frozen proof.
- Cards created later are never covered.

3.8 Transforms in a session (RV-9 b2, ES-9 b3, DO-2, RV-8 b2, D2-13, D4-6, D4-11)
- **Sources.** The Context Menu on the Proposed view. Decline → Transform on Formalize, Change, Add, Delete, vocabulary-term, declaration and typed items (one window for a group, RV-8). "Ask me instead" (RV-10): a group Decline → Transform of the items the choice relies on, with instructions prefilled "Ask me about: ‹choice›". This replaces D2-13's interim.
- **Submit transform in a session** is the reducer action queue-transform, one session-stack step (UN-4 4a):
  - declines the source items with option 'transform', Shaky-like: content stays in ws/, dependents in review become to be redone without revert, and accepted dependents need confirmation first (RV-5);
  - appends the QueuedTransform.
  It is allowed only in phase stage, while judging too (records-only, D2-27).
- **Cancel** changes nothing (TR-9 b: the items never left review).
- **An unchanged window** queues nothing; the items stay in review (TR-1 b).
- **drop-transform** returns the source items to review and removes the transform. **editTransform** reopens it as openDraft; Submit then sends queue-transform with `replaces`.
- **Setting a Transform-declined item back to review** is refused while its transform is queued: "Drop or edit its transform first."
- **Mid-stage Formalize** (formalizeStartProblems check 3, RV-9 b1 s3) refuses a target with a Transform-declined item, as for Shaky (D2-53). Whole-model step limits (3c1) also fix content declined Transform.
- **Suggested premises (D4-11).** A window on an Add premise item holds that premise and its target, read-only apart from the premise's sentence, Why and Lean statement. Its carry-out is a premise-edit unit, a records-only change of PersistedSession.premises. The item returns to review marked "updated", engine.judge checks the draft again (RV-1), and its Accept (holdAs) writes it with worded_by user for a typed sentence. Such a window never needs Claude.

3.9 Submit review with queued transforms (RV-12 b1, RV-5 b3, D2-57, D3-49, D4-4)
1. Gates are as in slices 2 and 3: nothing in review, the results shown, no step, not judging.
2. For each queued transform, telelean recomputes analyseTransform and transformImpact on the current state. It refuses when a draft names a card that no longer exists, when a problem appears, or when a dependent or needs-Claude set changed: "‹transform› needs a new look: open it again."
3. When the union of accepted cascades is not empty and the request is not confirmed, Submit answers needs-confirmation: "These accepted items return to review, because your transforms change what they rest on: …".
4. planSubmit builds the steps:
   - **Order:** transform steps in queue order (claude: false for those needing no Claude), then slice 2's Submit steps. Results in reworkResults and transform-origin Shaky or redo items join as affected; transform-origin items get a transform rework step.
   - **Take-out:** D2-57's take-out widens to every Shaky or to-be-redone item kept in ws/ that depends on a unit a transform touches, plus reworkResults. D3-49's keep set holds frozen content, transform and session-start reasons included.
5. The Submit write sets the confirmed cascade items in review and clears their `frozen` (R2-4: the person's confirmed cascade). Then come submit-take-out and queue-start, with the seal (D4-4). Even a Submit with only no-Claude transforms seals and opens stage + 1, never confirming.
6. Consent: when the session has no conversation yet (started unchanged) and the queue has a Claude step, the host asks egress consent first. The runner opens the conversation, with the context bundle, before the first Claude step.

3.10 The transform step (runner run/step.ts kind 'transform'; core judge; D4-3, D4-17)
1. **Typed write.** Commit step-start (rollback target, with StepScope.transform). Write the ledger `typed` entry to run.json. planTypedWrite on the head's model in mode 'session'. Files go into ws/, then commit `typed`. This is S0 for the limits, the two-value rule and existing-changed. A rework step skips the write.
2. **S0 check.** engine.check, purpose 'check', with the transform scope (one Lean job). It passes when:
   - G0 is clean;
   - every Lean error lies in the declarations of scope.dependents (statements and proofs left to Claude);
   - every typed declaration elaborates;
   - there is no other global finding.
   Otherwise the step fails at once ("Your transform “‹label›” does not build: ‹errors›"). Rollback goes to step-start, the ledger entry is dropped, the rest of the queue is not run, and the transform stays queued with lastFailure.
   TransformFreezes for the step's frozen fields come from the window: typed fields, copied-frozen fields and keep-empty. Each gets its value from this judgement where its facts exist, else `{ pending: true }` until the queue end (D4-20). `revalued` is set in the same run.json write, both computed only for the units' own targets and held names.
3. **No Claude.** A claude: false step ends `passed` here.
4. **Claude.** The turn begins `Step <i> of <n>: transform “<label>” (the person's transform)`, or `rework the transform “<label>” after the review`. Then come the window's cards with each field's state (frozen: value; fuzzy: fill; open: may change if the transform needs it; verbatim: write exactly), the trashed and new cards, slots, instructions quoted, the checkbox, dependents left to Claude, and slice 3's FROZEN and HELD sections.
   Tools:
   - check_lean, ask_user, request_unfreeze;
   - propose_arrow: into scope.arrowsInto cards, from any axiom or proposition of the subject; never into an axiom, a session target or a marked card; never a declined arrow or a cycle;
   - remove_arrow: only into open Dependencies; unfrozen, unselected, unused by any proof (B.3);
   - mark_proof_broken: only scope.dependents.proofs and proofs that no longer build in this step's state; never a session target (D3-47);
   - add_card { sentence, why, kind?, slot? }: a slot, or with mayAddCards, at most 10. Ledger `card` with optional target and kind; worded_by agent.
   Not allowed: freeze_statements, propose_assumption, delete_card.
   File edits: only scope.fields and vocab lines (G5 allowances limited to them), new vocabulary and definitions, and the statements of scope.dependents.statements.
5. **Gate** (gate-other semantics, no target, no comparator). judgeState runs with the transform scope:
   - step limits against S0, exempting only the scope's open set, Claude's ledger entries and the cards it added;
   - frozen and held checks (slice 3);
   - G5, with `type:` and `follows_from:` never by Claude;
   - B.3 (transform arrows) and B.4 (no .holds kind change except typed units; no theorem added, changed or completed);
   - new code `transform`: token `no-proofs` ("A transform step writes no proofs: remove ‹name›.", S8), token `typed-text`, token `slot`;
   - new-axiom (shape-passing vocabulary, an AXIOM card's new statement's .holds, typed units), stray-command, rejected-repeat, and DO-3's shaky-identical for a rework.
   Every inference is judged (RV-11); other inferences' findings never count against Claude.
   finish status: 'done' | 'cannot' (FinishStatus additions). 'cannot' passes if the gate passes, with the gap reported (A3).
6. **Rollback** (all or nothing). A step that gives up, is cancelled or fails goes back to step-start: the typed write too, its ledger entries, and its TransformFreezes and revalues. The transform stays queued, with Retry step. A rerun writes again.
7. **Step end:** ledger `created` (phase statements) and `changed` entries (3c1's origins).
8. **Queue end (reconcile, 4b1).**
   - **Auto-accept.** Every typed:<card> draft that has a unit from this queue's typed entries is created or set accepted, how 'yours', with `frozen` from that judgement. The condition: every RV-5 dependency outside the typed set is accepted, as a fixpoint over the queue's typed drafts. Otherwise it is in review, marked typed-by-you, and needs only a plain Accept.
   - **Transform-declined source items:** back to review, marked "updated" when their key changed (slice 2's F5 rule generalised to 'transform'). With no draft left: withdrawn, replaced-by-transform. A trashed Claude Add item becomes declined (reject), so it is never proposed again.
   - **Pending TransformFreezes** take their value from this judgement; a verbatim one only if its text matches. Questions lose sources whose arrow a typed unit removed, with the report line "“‹L›” left the question for “‹T›”: you removed its arrow."
   - The judge-apply re-runs frozenFindings after setting values and revalues (slice 3 §3.5).

3.11 Ownership, revert, classes (4b1; D4-1, D4-18)
- **computeItems.** A difference B→W is owned by `typed:<card>` when a live `typed` unit lists it and W's value equals the unit's. Units are block lines (entries), whole declarations, blocks and arrows. Every other difference keeps slices 2/3's rules: Claude's card:, decl:, arrow: items, or unowned. So typed and Claude content of one card are owned field by field. Later typed entries supersede earlier ones unit by unit. Live typed entries are those not rolled back.
- **planItemRevert** becomes field-precise for card: Change items: B's lines of only the item's own lines. A typed item's revert restores B's version of its units: field lines, declarations, blocks restored, arrows.
- **classify:** typed items get their classes for display but never need their own Accept (RV-7 b5). D2-23 never returns them. The backstop's own-accept and class codes exempt how 'yours'. isMeaningItem is false for typed, so it never keeps the results hidden.
- **itemDeps:** typed items join RV-5 like any item: mentions, rule 3 for arrows to or from Claude's added cards, rule 5 for deletions.
- **Decline options for typed items:** Reject or Transform; no Shaky ("Claude may not rework what you typed"). D3-48 lists their transform-frozen units, offering only [Unfreeze them and decline] [Cancel]. A cascade that takes a typed item out makes it withdrawn, not to be redone; un-reject brings it back in review.

3.12 Freezes (4b2)
- **effectiveFreezes** adds:
  - session-start entries (§3.7);
  - TransformFreeze entries with their values; pending ones have no expectation, and the step limits fix them;
  - `revalued.keys` replace the `{ from: 'base' }` expectation of standing, foreign and session-start entries of that key, and own freezes' values are rewritten in place;
  - `revalued.held` replaces every non-accepted holder's held expectation of that name. Accepted items leave accepted instead (RV-5 b3, §3.9).
- Only typed writes add to `revalued`; Claude never can.
- frozenChangesOf treats transform rows like own rows. buildFreezesView adds the banner and mode.
- FZ-8 rows come out of the whole-state rule: transform reasons give 'frozen' rows with keep at Apply, and at Exit only when the value is B's.

3.13 Backstop and final check (4b1)
applyBackstop re-derives typed ownership from B, F and the ledger. A typed item must be accepted. Its content key in F equals its accepted key ('content-changed' otherwise). Exceptions for typed units only:
- G5 for `type:` and `follows_from:`;
- B.4 for theorem→axiom of P→A;
- new-axiom rule 6: an AXIOM card's .holds made by a typed kind change;
- arrows owned by typed items.
judgeState('final') and EN-2's checks need no other change.

3.14 Persistence and reload (ES-6)
- Outside a session: the host's draft store.
- In a session: openDraft and transforms in run.json. The typed write runs inside its step: an interrupted step is resumed or cancelled as in slice 2, and Cancel step takes the whole transform back.
- recover() needs no new path. A crash between the ledger write and the commit is undone by the step's rollback.

3.15 Protocol and RunManager (core protocol.ts, 4c; runner run/types.ts)
- **Webview → host messages** (all in RUN_MESSAGE_TYPES, with hand validators, fresh objects and size limits):
  - openTransform { cards, vocab?, from?, runId?, stage? };
  - saveTransformDraft { draft, runId? };
  - checkTransform { draftId, revision, runId? };
  - submitTransform { draftId, revision, confirmed?: { cascade?, dependents?, glow?, kinds? }, runId?, stage? };
  - cancelTransform { draftId, runId? };
  - dropTransform { runId, stage, transform, confirmed? };
  - editTransform { runId, stage, transform }.
- **Host → webview:** `transform { draft|null, analysis?, checking? }` outside a session; inside one, SessionView.openDraft.
- **RunManager:** transformStart(r: { subject; draft; analysis; mode: 'unchanged'|'claude' }), transformOpen, transformSave, transformCheck, transformSubmit (queue), transformCancel, transformDrop, transformEdit. Each resolves after its run.json write (D2-74).
- While a step runs, open, save and check are allowed; queue, drop and edit are refused with D2-62's text.
- apply-transform is an ES-9-locked board action.

4. AUTOPILOT DECISIONS (each: AUTOPILOT DECISION, alternative, reversal)
- **D4-1 Typed content.** What you type is one typed:<card> item per card, accepted as yours when its dependencies are accepted. Claude's copied content stays in Claude's items.
  - Alt: a moving baseline Y = B + typed, with items computed against Y (ES-7's "against the base" would then be narrowed, and typed Lean naming Claude's vocabulary breaks Y's build); or typed units folded into Claude's per-card items.
  - Reverse: drop typedKey and route units to card:, decl: and arrow: items created with how 'yours'.
- **D4-2 No run while drafting.** Outside a session the draft is the host's; the session with its base and session-start freezes starts at Submit transform; a stale draft is refused.
  - Alt: ES-3's provisional run from window opening (locks the board, holds B and the freezes).
  - Reverse: start a run with phase 'drafting' at openTransform.
- **D4-3 One step per transform, all or nothing.** Every transform is a queue step (typed write, check, Claude when needed); one that does not pass is taken back whole and stays queued.
  - Alt: keep the typed write when only Claude's part fails.
  - Reverse: roll back to the newest passing commit at or after S0 when S0 passed.
- **D4-4 Submit seals and opens a stage.** A Submit that carries out transforms seals and always opens a new stage (narrows RV-12 b2 and D2-54).
  - Alt: carry out no-Claude transforms and go straight to confirming, with Back to review undoing them.
  - Reverse: make the typed write an undoable decision commit and let planSubmit choose confirming.
- **D4-5 TR-12 scratch and verbatim statements.** TR-12 (b) checks against your files at the model root. Names not in them are written verbatim by Claude, enforced by `typed-text`, and typed vocabulary must elaborate now.
  - Alt: check against the working copy (leaks hidden lemma names, needs mirror switching); or refuse undefined names.
  - Reverse: run the scratch in the session mirror and drop `typed-text`.
- **D4-6 Decline → Transform declines at queueing.** The items are declined only when the transform is queued (Shaky-like); Cancel changes nothing; back to review is refused while its transform is queued.
  - Alt: decline when the window opens and undo on Cancel.
- **D4-7 Claude's copied values start open.** Values copied from Claude start open and marked, refining TR-4, which protects your own Lean.
  - Alt: TR-4 literally (freezes Claude's proposal).
  - Reverse: makeTransformDraft's starting states.
- **D4-8 Make it pending after Apply.** "Make it pending" (TR-14 d, D3-10) is the board's Mark pending after Apply.
  - Alt: a Proof broken Accept option with an in-session due write like the premise write.
- **D4-9 D2-15 kept.** No splits or merges in Formalize-origin rework; transform-origin rework follows that transform's TR-7 setting; splits of your cards go through Decline → Transform.
  - Alt: lift it with add_card in Submit steps.
- **D4-10 No in-session D-11 rewrite.** An in-session kind change needing D-11's rewrite is refused.
  - Alt: typed rewrites of dependents.
- **D4-11 Suggested premises edit their draft.** Transforming one edits its draft only (sentence, Why, Lean); it is re-checked and accepted with holdAs.
  - Alt: not offered (narrows the user's TRANSFORM 9); or make it a new card of yours.
- **D4-12 Fuzzy-sentence new cards are slots.** add_card fills them; no typed arrow may involve a slot.
  - Alt: require every new card's sentence.
- **D4-13 Direct path freezes typed fields.** The direct path freezes typed fields of existing cards as standing freezes (FROZEN 1, TR-5, extending D3-44); it does not freeze new cards, kind, Dependencies or proof.
  - Alt: no freezes (ES-3's "its freezes are undone" literally).
- **D4-14 Session-start freezes cover whole cards.** They cover every non-window card, vocabulary included, all fields and Dependencies.
  - Alt: axiom and proposition cards only.
- **D4-15 Proposed view only.** In a session, Transform cards… works only on the Proposed view and from the review list.
- **D4-16 Session targets are protected.** Their proof is locked, they cannot be trashed, and their statement changes only when B has no proof of them, with the Result reworked in the same queue.
  - Alt: allow Results to turn into Proof broken (against D3-47).
- **D4-17 What a transform step may not do.** It writes no proofs and kinds, has no freeze_statements, propose_assumption or delete_card, and finishes 'done' or 'cannot'.
- **D4-18 Typed items' options.** No Shaky; they are not meaning items for the reveal; a plain Accept; withdrawn when a cascade takes them out.
- **D4-19 TR-13 choices.** In a session the choices are 'claude' (unfrozen) or 'delete'; 'broken' and 'rewrite' exist outside sessions only; references come in slice 5.
- **D4-20 When typed units get their freeze values.** From the first judgement with their facts (S0, else the queue end).
  - Residual: an instance Claude adds in the same step that changes how a typed declaration elaborates is reviewed as its own item (S5), and a later Reject of it is caught by D3-48.
- **D4-21 Where Transform is offered.** Not on Results or arrow items (slice 2) nor on Proof broken items; yes on Add premise (D4-11) and typed items. A typed sentence also updates its statement's docstring mirror, which goes into Claude's item when the statement holds Claude's content (cosmetic residual).
